Z||000010||MoneypitGT||12-14-2001||10:32 PM||||Thanks for all the comments, It took a lot of time, and money (lifters alone are $300) to get it to where it is. As far as stats go, I am hoping for around 280hp at the wheels, running about 8psi. As for the IDI cover, didn't get there quite yet, but it will be changed, don't worry.<BR> Chris<P>------------------<BR>  <B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>Turbo Q4 GT Project||||reg||14
Z||000011||Eric_PA||12-14-2001||11:16 PM||||Chris,<BR>Are you going with the stock pistons? Also, what turbo did you decide to go with. I am looking to possible go the Q4 route again, but this time go all the way through with it.<P>Eric||||reg||1
Z||000012||Ayrow||12-15-2001||02:58 AM||||Ok, maybe I'm a little to new to this.<P>That is a beautiful engine.<P>I hope this is not stupid question (although I'm afraid it is) but is that a four, six,  or Eight cylinder engine?<P>I'm not sure if the "Quad" represents the cylinder count or maybe the valve count.<P>Thanks,<P>Ayrow<BR>||||reg||5
Z||000013||artherd||12-15-2001||03:44 AM||||HAH!  The individual cam castings DO kind of look like a very little narrow angle V12  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>But that motor is a 4-banger.  Kind of a hot one, stock is 180bhp (with a few stock 190bhp variants) and more can be had quite easially before you ever have to go turbo.<P>I think George (cadero2dmax) was pulling 230bhp+ NA out of his motor on the 88 racer...<P>Best!<BR>Ben<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.cartsys.com/fiero/sig1.jpeg">    <BR>Ben Cannon<BR>88 Formula, T-top, Metalic Red           &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;"Every Man Dies, not every man really Lives"<BR>88 Formula, Northstar, Silver                    &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;-Mel Gibson, "Braveheart"||||reg||3
Z||000014||Standard||12-15-2001||01:17 PM||||George was also running 13:1 compression  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>Chris, what kinda parts did ya use to rebuild it?  Drop the compression?  What kinda lifters did you get?  Even the Mantapart lifters are only $250 for the set.<P>Ayrow, the Quad refers to 4 valves per cylinder.||||reg||1
Z||000015||MoneypitGT||12-15-2001||06:47 PM||||Stock pistons, stock HO cams, (both were perfect) Clevite bearings, Gm rings(which are suuposed to be the best, not that you have an option)all new sensors, and Blue racer lifters, they were actually about $270w/tax, which I didn't know Mantapart came down on their price, I thought they were a lot higher but oh well. Turbo is a T-3, big ol' intercooler (cutting out the trunk)custom intake, A/C eliminator, MSD Dis-2, Apex boost controller, um I think that is it. Compression is a little high but if I manage the timing and keep it from leaning out it should be good, (just have to pray to the headgasket gods everynight.) I know friends of mine that have done much worse and faired well (so far) but either way, I guess we will find out.<BR> Chris<P>------------------<BR>  <B>Check out my site at:</B>   <A HREF="http://www.customdynamix.com" TARGET=_blank>www.customdynamix.com</A> <BR>Turbo Q4 GT Project||||reg||14
